Subject: [PATCH 3/4] refactor(nemotron): drop the vision_final_layernorm
 completeness check

535487a0c made NemotronH_Omni_Reasoning_V3.load_weights raise on its
first call unless both vision_projector.vision_final_layernorm.weight
and .bias were loaded. That checks 2 of ~43k tensors. Nothing beneath
it checks the rest: NemotronH_Nano_VL_V2.load_weights drops unknown
prefixes with no else branch, NemotronHForCausalLM.load_weights only
logs (or, for expert weights, silently skips) unmatched names, the
RADIO loader's returned set is discarded, and DefaultModelLoader never
compares loaded against expected parameters. A check that covers two
tensors does not make the load complete, and it needed a first-call
flag to stay quiet during RL bucketed syncs. Remove it, the flag, and
the loaded set.

Kept: rerouting those two tensors into self.vision_final_layernorm,
and the raise when the checkpoint carries them but the model was built
without the layer -- a structure mismatch, not a completeness check.

